    "turn_text": "No, actually, ever since I was a teenager, I started volunteering on campaigns. So in high school, I would ride my bike to campaign headquarters, congressional campaign on Long Island. against Congressman Norman Lent, who was the Republican incumbent at the time. And so I volunteered for that and I became a Democratic commitment as a teenager. And so politics had always been in my bloodstream. And I chose George Washington University for two reasons. Number one, It was in Washington DC, in my view, the capital of American politics. And number two, its faculty, many of them had practical experience working in various federal departments, working in campaigns, working in the White House. And I wanted that kind of practical and experiential instruction.",
