    "turn_text": "Yeah, I'll give you a very specific example. We had a staffer who was working on transportation issues, and I was a newly elected member in a district that had been held by Republican Rick Lazio. Now, let me set the stage for you. This was a very Republican district. Rick Lazio was winning with 70, 75 percent of the vote. He decided to leave the House to run against Hillary Clinton for the Senate. I jumped into the race, had a brutal Democratic primary just squeaked by in that primary, and was now in one of the top tier open seat elections in the country in 2000. Again, representing a very Republican district that, you know, it was a waterfront district along something called the Great South Bay. I think that they believe that Rick Lazio could walk back and forth across the Great South Bay.",
