    "turn_text": "You can't just snuff them out because then, you know, what's the use of them coming to work? You know, you want to look if they were, as you said in the question, if he had done it again, if they were repeated mistakes, yeah, well, you know, see you later, but you got to give people a chance. I'll give you, if I may, I'll give you another example of what I thought was really bad staffing. Again, you know, I talked about the importance of marrying legislative to resonance back home. I had been convinced to introduce legislation by a bunch of amateur radio operators in my district who were concerned that many condominium developments and co-op developments in New York were banning amateur radio towers. And they said, you know, back in the day, these towers were 40 feet high. So yeah, you want to ban them. But now you could operate an amateur radio with a tower inside your house. That's about three feet high. So we decided to introduce legislation that would have",
