  {
    "episode_id": 49869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "Pizza, pizza, pizza. So I think walking in the shoes of a member you realize just you're being pulled by the district staff versus the Washington staff, by the press secretary versus the constituent services director, by your colleagues, by your caucus, by the leadership, by your donors, by the finance team, by the campaign team. And so it is a surreal existence where you are constantly, as a principal, as a member, feeling like you're getting torn apart. I think that would be very useful for staffers to kind of understand how to achieve some kind of balance that makes the member of Congress's life a little bit more sane.",
